--- every emulated catalog view has a pg_class row in pg_catalog and pg_attribute rows
pg_attribute|r|pg_catalog|1
pg_class|r|pg_catalog|1
pg_enum|r|pg_catalog|1
pg_namespace|r|pg_catalog|1
pg_proc|r|pg_catalog|1
pg_range|r|pg_catalog|1
pg_type|r|pg_catalog|1
--- pg_type round-trips in full, including the leading oid column, and oid columns are numbers
UInt32	UInt32	String	26	oid	0
UInt32	UInt32	String	1007	_int4	23
--- and so does pg_attribute, whose own rows describe the catalog views themselves
1
